    {
      "id": 21765,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "Researchers identified endpoints that were vulnerable to reflected XSS, due to insufficient input sanitization. This could allow malicious client-side content to be rendered by the app, which could affect a user's session, browser, or the contents of the page itself. The issue was resolved by applying a specific filter on the input and returning it as a sanitized string. ",
